65,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at our options, Candidate A provides a lasting catalogue and relies on data, while Candidate B requires the spectroscopy suite we know is unreliable. Candidate C involves animals, and D requires the full glasshouses.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, you're right! Candidate A sounds perfect! It's a catalogue, which @Daisuke said lasts a long time, and it doesn't need the glasshouses or expensive animal fees! It's the winner for sure!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. Candidate A is a catalogue-style project, which my research showed has the most lasting impact. It avoids the risks of breeding colonies and the glasshouse bottleneck. It seems like the most reliable choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, you nailed it. B needs that broken spectroscopy suite, C is a gamble with animals, and D is stuck in a full glasshouse. A is the only one that actually has a chance of finishing. I'm voting A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Minako,,"The analysis is conclusive. Candidate D is impossible due to glasshouse bookings, and Candidate B is too risky given the instrumentation failures. Candidate A aligns with our available computational strengths and repository efficiency. I vote for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is rare to find such harmony in a deliberation. We have aligned our resources, our risks, and our goals. I, too, shall cast my vote for Candidate A, for it is the most sustainable path.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I'm so happy we all agree! It's like we solved a big mystery together! Candidate A is definitely the best fit for everything we found. I'm voting for A too! Yay!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel confident in this. Candidate A is the only one that avoids all the pitfalls we discovered. I'm voting for A as well.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Takumi,,No point in arguing when the facts are this clear. A is the only one that doesn't rely on a miracle. I'm sticking with A.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Minako,,The logic is sound and the evidence is overwhelming. Candidate A is the only proposal that is compatible with our current constraints and strengths. I maintain my vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Servas,,"Since we have reached a complete consensus based on the evidence, I believe our work here is done. May this project flourish and provide a lasting benefit to the scientific community.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I agree! It was so much fun working with everyone! I'm super glad we found the perfect project. I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
